        "caption": "The Copano Bay Fishing Pier is 2500 feet long on the south side of the bay and 6190 feet long on the north side. This is the north side pier looking southwest with the causeway of Texas State Highway 35 on the left. The piers were built in 1931 as a causeway for State Highway 35. When the new causeway was built, the middle of the old bridge was removed, and the two piers were left. Two spans near the end of the south pier collapsed in 2017. A structural survey deemed the piers unsafe, and they were demolished in late summer 2020.",
